Lota's physics patch (ADR 001, section 2): the only change Lota makes to
LÖVE's engine. LÖVE's src/modules/physics/box2d is the one module whose
engine classes hold Lua: methods that read and push the Lua stack, the
contact, filter, query, and raycast callbacks that call Lua functions, and
user data kept as Lua references. Without Lua none of it compiles. This
patch replaces each with C++: a method that pushed its results returns
them, through LÖVE's own convention of output parameters (as
Body::getPosition does) or a std::vector where their number varies; a
method that read its arguments from the stack takes them as parameters;
and what a Lua Reference held is an object of Reference.h's interfaces,
which the binding implements. LÖVE's statements, their order, and their
arithmetic are otherwise left as they are. CMake applies it to a copy of
the module at configure time (ext/lota/engine/CMakeLists.txt); vendor/love
is never written to.

